<title>GERMANY: Thyssen H1 pre-tax profit up 81 pct.</title>
<headline>Thyssen H1 pre-tax profit up 81 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     631     vs 349</p>
<p>    Group sales				  17,922  vs 18,423</p>
<p>    Group investment			   1,268   vs 822</p>
<p>    Group incoming orders		    17,800  vs 18,100</p>
<p>    Group workforce (headcount)	    112,893 vs 122,659</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German engineering, steel and telecommunications group is Thyssen AG.</p>
<p>The company said the rise in earnings was partly due to extraordinary effects. Excluding extraordinary effects, group profit rose by 22 percent, the company said. The drop in incoming orders was explained by disinvestments. Calculated on a comparable basis, orders rose one percent, due mainly to a rise in foreign orders. Group sales adjusted for disinvestments rose by two percent, Thyssen said.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
